{"clock":7,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","forge_id":"6241141593","number":"34","url":"https://github.com/guilbep/bimble/issues/34"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","field":"title","value":"Layouts in the navigator: make and export sheets"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","field":"body","value":"The navigator's Layouts section only opens the Plan… window today.\n\nTo do: New sheet, drag views onto it (scale per viewport), move them on the paper, title block fields, live preview, export PDF/SVG. Sheets listed like views, with Duplicate/Delete.\n\nNeeds: sheets in the model.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","field":"status","value":"open"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","field":"labels","value":""}},{"kind":"seen","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","field":"comment:6683650730","value":"Pierre (6 Nov), what a layout must be:\n- **opened in the main view** (like the plan preview, but in place of the 3D/2D view), chosen from **Layouts** in the navigator;\n- **a static page** (the paper sheet at scale) that is **interactive**: select items on it, **add dimensions (cotations)**, **add text**;\n- **drag and drop views** from the navigator into the layout, then move them on the page.\n\nSo the sheet is drawn live in the main view from its vector items (not a picture), with selection, handles and snapping; its export is the same items as PDF/SVG.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794138675,"data":{"issue":"94f2e5c9ab1411662889347d39b5efa518e6ca89","field":"comment:6684456923","value":"Decided (Pierre, 6 Nov):\n- **Dimensions belong to the view** (as in Revit): they measure the model, follow it when it changes, and show wherever the view is placed and in the view on screen. They are saved with the view (`.bimble` / side file), associated to element GlobalIds and snap points.\n- **Text: both.** Text placed inside a viewport belongs to the view (e.g. a label on an element); text placed outside belongs to the sheet (notes, titles).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"}}]}